# Overview

**Software Title:** Study Time Tracker (Personal Task Planner)

**Software Description:**
This application is a dual-interface study logging system built in **Kotlin**. Designed as the third module for CSE 310 (Applied Programming), this project connects directly with my previous coursework[cite: 1, 3, 4, 5]. In Module 1, I created a Study Time Tracker in C#[cite: 3], and in Module 2, I analyzed that study log data using R[cite: 4].

For Module 3, I developed a software solution in Kotlin that manages study sessions via both a **Command Line Interface (CLI)** and a **Graphical User Interface (GUI)**[cite: 1, 5]. Both interfaces read from and write to the exact same shared `study_logs.csv` dataset, enabling cross-language data integration and tracking throughout the course[cite: 3, 4, 5].

**Software Purpose:**
The purpose of this software is to help students record, organize, and analyze time spent during academic Sprints. It tracks session dates, work categories (e.g., Planning, Research, Implementation, Troubleshooting, Documentation, Video Production, Publishing), descriptions, and hours spent[cite: 3, 4, 5]. It calculates totals, session averages, and category percentage breakdowns to prevent procrastination and support structured time management[cite: 3, 4, 5, 6].
